  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscPhys 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'You notice that many patients with the same type of cancer stop responding
    to a standard treatment after about six months. You share this observation with
    a research team, sparking ideas for new drugs that could work once resistance
    develops.


    <b>In this scenario, what role is the physician playing in drug
    discovery?</b>'
  explanation: "Physicians play an important role early in the research process by
    sharing what they see while caring for patients. By noticing patterns\u2014such
    as how a disease changes over time, how well treatments work, or what side effects
    patients experience\u2014doctors can help spark new research ideas. This early
    input helps researchers focus on the most important patient needs and develop
    treatments that are more likely to make a real difference in people\u2019s lives."
  correctAnswer: Identifying patterns in patient care that may inspire new research
  incorrectAnswer1: Identifying specific parts of the disease that a new treatment
    could target
  incorrectAnswer2: Deciding whether a new treatment would be realistic and manageable
    for patients to use
  incorrectAnswer3: Deciding how often and how much of a treatment patients might
    receive in a future study
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
